=== WORKER_SCAFFOLDED ===

internal/worker/unit_drift_validator.go (~25 KB):

  Type:       UnitDriftValidator
  Constructors:
    NewUnitDriftValidator(*database.DB, *database.VehicleRepo)
        — production wiring; uses pgxpool for SELECT; uses
          vehicleRepoAdapter to flatten []*models.Vehicle → []int64.
    NewUnitDriftValidatorWithDeps(vehicleLister, signalReader)
        — testable; lets tests inject in-memory data without a DB.

  Public API:
    Start(ctx, Options) — long-running cron loop (default 24h
        cadence). Immediate first pass on startup so a deploy
        doesn't have to wait for the next tick. Designed for
        resilience.SafeGoLoop wiring.
    Run(ctx, Options)   — single pass. Returns nil even when drift
        is found (drift is a logged/counted finding, not a caller-
        visible error). Returns non-nil only for genuine pipeline
        failures (DB unreachable, ctx cancelled).

  Drift checks (all read-only SELECT against signal_log):
    checkSpeed           — VehicleSpeed (canonical SI m/s) vs.
        great-circle distance over time from LocationLatitude /
        LocationLongitude. Requires ≥ 10 ratios above the noise
        floor; mean ratio must be in [0.85, 1.15] or the counter
        fires with kind="speed".
    checkOdometer        — Odometer trip-mode delta (m) vs.
        ∫ VehicleSpeed dt (trapezoidal). Same ±15% threshold.
        Fires with kind="odometer".
    checkTemperature     — Inside/OutsideTemp range sanity. Sample
        outside [-50°C, +80°C] is the canonical fingerprint of a
        F→C unit-context drop. Fires with kind="temp_high" when
        ≥ 50%% of samples are implausible.
    checkUnitHistoryCanary — vehicle_unit_history latest-row age.
        Fires the warn-tier tesla_unit_history_canary_total with
        reason="no_history_7d" when the most-recent row is older
        than 7 days OR there are zero rows.

  Metrics (cardinality bounded by fleet × small closed sets):
    tesla_unit_drift_suspected_total{vehicle_id, kind}
        kind ∈ {speed, odometer, temp_high}
    tesla_unit_history_canary_total{vehicle_id, reason}
        reason ∈ {no_history_7d}

  Dry-run gate: when Options.DryRun=true, the validator skips
  every counter Inc but still emits zerolog WARN findings — used
  by --dry-run for forensic triage without poisoning the alert
  pipeline.

