=== CLI_SCAFFOLDED ===

cmd/unit-drift-validator/main.go (~5.6 KB):

  Flags:
    --once               run a single pass and exit (default: long-
                         running loop)
    --dry-run            log findings WITHOUT incrementing the
                         tesla_unit_drift_suspected_total counter
    --vehicle ID         limit to one vehicle (default: full fleet)
    --lookback DUR       how far back into signal_log each pass
                         reads (default: 1h)
    --cron-interval DUR  cadence for the long-running loop (default:
                         24h; ignored when --once)
    --version            print build version and exit

  Operator credential gate (REQUIRED): refuses to launch if
  TESLASYNC_OPERATOR_TOKEN is unset or whitespace-only. Identical
  sentinel to cmd/resubscribe; same rotation policy.

  Audit trail: zerolog INFO 'event=unit_drift_validator.start'
  before any DB read (operator, once, dry_run, vehicle, lookback,
  cron_interval, version) and 'event=unit_drift_validator.end' on
  exit.

  Exit semantics:
    0  success (full pass complete OR --version OR clean shutdown)
    2  flag parse failure
    3  TESLASYNC_OPERATOR_TOKEN unset
    4  config.Load failed
    5  database.New failed
    6  Run() returned a non-context-cancellation error

