=== SERVER_WIRING ===

cmd/teslasync/main.go: 10-line block added at line 624,
immediately after the gas-price-worker wiring and before the
health-watchdog block. Pattern matches the existing maintenance-
worker / gas-price-worker wiring exactly:

  driftVehicleRepo := database.NewVehicleRepo(db)
  driftValidator := worker.NewUnitDriftValidator(db, driftVehicleRepo)
  resilience.SafeGoLoop(ctx, "unit-drift-validator", func(loopCtx context.Context) {
      driftValidator.Start(loopCtx, worker.Options{})
  })
  log.Info().Msg("unit-drift validator started")

A separate VehicleRepo instance is constructed (driftVehicleRepo)
because the existing vehicleRepo at line 339 is scoped to the
live-signal-store warmup block and not in scope at line 624.
NewVehicleRepo holds no connection state — repos are cheap stateless
struct literals — so two instances cost nothing.

